<BaseLayout
  title="Tirso / Antón Martín walk north to four Sol doors before 14:00 | Dubliners"
  description="Sunday 8 Nov ~13:00: already at Tirso de Molina or Antón Martín (L1, south of Sol)? Walk north on Magdalena / Cruz / Espoz y Mina to Victoria 6, Espoz y Mina 7 and Pasaje de Matheu 4 before 14:00. Street walk, metres, Maps."
  path={PATH}
  lang="en"
  hreflang={{ en: PATH, es: PATH_ES }}
  ogImage="/images/facade.jpg"
  extraJsonLd={[articleLd, faqLd]}
>
  <section class="hero hero-compact" data-show-until={SHOW_UNTIL}>
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb current="Tirso / Antón Martín: walk north to the four Sol doors" schema />
      <h1>Tirso de Molina / Antón Martín: walk north to the four Sol doors before 14:00</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Saturday is over. You are not on Plaza Mayor, not on Preciados with shopping bags, not in Atocha’s concourse, and not surfacing inside Sol Metro.
        <strong>You are already south of Sol</strong> — Plaza de Tirso de Molina or Plaza de Antón Martín, Line 1.
        Walk <strong>north on Calle de la Magdalena, then Calle de la Cruz, then Espoz y Mina</strong>.
        Pin the four sister doors before Four Corner opens at 14:00 with sports screens (about one hour from 13:00; not open before). Maps below.
      </p>
      <p class="small">En español: <a href={withBase(PATH_ES)} hreflang="es" lang="es">Tirso de Molina / Antón Martín: al norte, las cuatro puertas de Sol antes de las 14:00</a></p>
      <FanWeekendCtas lang="en" findHref="/visit/" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>This is a north walk from two L1 plazas, not Sol station, not Atocha, not Callao, not Plaza Mayor</h2>
      <p>
        Other pages already cover the first Metro <em>into</em> Sol (platform to door on the square), Atocha Cercanías one stop,
        Callao–Preciados south, Plaza Mayor’s east arcade, a Sol hotel’s first street, and Barajas.
        This page is only for the person <strong>already on the street at Tirso de Molina or Antón Martín</strong>
        who needs the north heading, metres, and which door to pin before 14:00.
        Do not re-promote Saturday 18:00–19:00 as still on.
      </p>

      <h2>Tirso or Antón Martín → Magdalena north → Cruz → Espoz y Mina</h2>
      <p>
        Stay on the surface. Do not ride L1 one more stop into Sol unless you want the station-to-door page instead.
        From <strong>Plaza de Tirso de Molina</strong> walk <strong>north on Calle de la Magdalena</strong>.
        Magdalena runs into <strong>Calle de la Cruz</strong> — keep north toward Sol.
        Then Espoz y Mina (number 7 twice), Pasaje de Matheu (the covered cut-through off that street) and Calle de la Victoria.
        From <strong>Plaza de Antón Martín</strong> the same Magdalena is the north street; you pass Tirso on the way.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>From Plaza de Tirso de Molina, north on Magdalena / Cruz.</strong>
          Espoz y Mina 7: <strong>6–8 min / 450–600 m</strong>.
          Pasaje de Matheu 4: <strong>7–9 min / 500–650 m</strong>.
          Victoria 6: <strong>7–9 min / 500–680 m</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>From Plaza de Antón Martín, north on Magdalena through Tirso.</strong>
          Add about <strong>4–6 min / 300–400 m</strong>.
          Espoz y Mina 7: <strong>10–13 min / 750–950 m</strong>.
          Matheu 4 and Victoria 6: <strong>11–14 min / 800–1000 m</strong>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        From about 13:00 it is <strong>about one hour</strong> until Four Corner opens at 14:00.
        You have time to walk it. Pin Victoria 6 for that hour. Do not camp a closed door on Calle de la Victoria before then.
      </p>

      <h2>Before 14:00 — which door is even open</h2>
      <p>
        Four Corner opens <strong>Sunday 8 November from 14:00 until late, with sports screens</strong>.
        Not before 14:00. We do not list which game is on there — ask at the door.
        O’Reilly’s usual from 11:30 (Pasaje de Matheu 4). Dubliners usual Sunday from 12:00 (Espoz y Mina 7).
        Walk Magdalena now; sit the first sister that is open; be on Victoria for the 14:00 open.
        O’Connell’s usual Sunday door is 14:00 (today’s listing also from 12:00 — we do not invent).
        Premier League from 15:00 (Palace–Liverpool, Sunderland–Chelsea, Brighton–Brentford, Ipswich–Bournemouth),
        United–Villa 17:30, NFL afternoon/evening, and Atlético–Barcelona 21:00 sit on the same streets after that — coordinate, do not substitute.
        Named listings: Dubliners <a href={withBase('/whats-on/')}>What’s On</a> only. Ask which screen — not every game on every screen.
      </p>

      <h2>South of Sol to three streets — addresses</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Four Corner — Calle de la Victoria 6, 28012 Madrid</strong> (pin for 14:00; sports screens; not open before).
          About 7–9 min from Tirso / 11–14 min from Antón Martín.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar — Pasaje de Matheu 4, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Covered passage off Espoz y Mina. Usual from 11:30. About 7–9 min from Tirso.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dubliners — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          About 6–8 min from Tirso. Sunday from 12:00. Named screens on What’s On — ask which game is on.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Connell’s — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid</strong> (Maps listing: O’Connell St).
          Same street number as Dubliners, different door. Usual Sunday 14:00 (today also listed from 12:00). Meeting point; we do not invent its board.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <OriginalFourBars lang="en" when="sunday" findHref="/visit/" />

      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <dl class="faq">
        <dt><strong>At Tirso or Antón Martín this afternoon. Which way before 14:00?</strong></dt>
        <dd>North on Magdalena, then Cruz, then Espoz y Mina. Pin Victoria 6 for 14:00. Then Matheu 4 and Espoz y Mina 7 twice. Street walk — do not ride into Sol unless you want the station page.</dd>
        <dt><strong>How far from Tirso / Antón Martín to the four doors?</strong></dt>
        <dd>Tirso north: Espoz y Mina 7 6–8 min / 450–600 m; Matheu 4 7–9 min / 500–650 m; Victoria 6 7–9 min / 500–680 m. Antón Martín add 4–6 min / 300–400 m. Do not wait on Victoria 6 before 14:00.</dd>
        <dt><strong>It is ~13:00. Is Four Corner open?</strong></dt>
        <dd>No. From 14:00, sports screens — about one hour from now. O’Reilly’s from 11:30; Dubliners from 12:00. Do not wait on Victoria 6 before 14:00.</dd>
      </dl>

      <LinkHub
        heading="h2"
        groups={[
          {
            title: 'From Tirso / Antón Martín this Sunday',
            until: SHOW_UNTIL,
            items: [
              { href: '/', label: 'FIND US — Dubliners home' },
              { href: '/visit/', label: 'GET DIRECTIONS — visit / hours' },
              { href: '/4-bars-one-fan-weekend/', label: 'MEET US NEAR SOL' },
              { href: '/last-hour-before-four-corner-1400/', label: 'Last 60 minutes: sit O’Reilly’s and Dubliners, walk at 14:00' },
              { href: '/four-corner-opens-sunday-1400/', label: 'Four Corner Sunday 14:00' },
              { href: PATH_ES, label: 'Tirso / Antón Martín: al norte a las cuatro puertas de Sol', note: 'En español', hreflang: 'es', lang: 'es' },
            ],
          },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
  <FixtureAntiStale />
</BaseLayout>
